      "body": "In DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash decode, each mixture-of-experts (MoE) layer runs a separate reduction of the routed-expert outputs and then the tensor-parallel all-reduce. This draft folds the reduction into the decode all-reduce kernel, which already fuses the post step of the mHC (hyper-connection) residual mixing, so one launch and one pass over the hidden states are saved per layer.\r\n\r\n- Predicted from the decode traces (MI355X, tensor parallel on 4 GPUs): about 1-2% less decode time per step without shared-expert fusion, less with it.\r\n- Conservative expectation: about 0.5% higher output throughput.\r\n- Status: draft without code.\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #37201699614](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37201699614)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37201699470](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37201699470)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
